          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.898,
            0.118,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": "158"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.883,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": "Under special conditions, it might also fall as hail or snow. Aavi enjoys the rain and creates a poem. You can complete the poem and present it in your class."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.177,
            0.653,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "**I wonder, oh! I wonder so, Which path does water choose to go? I wonder, oh! I wonder so, When does it snow? I wonder, oh! I got a wonder call, How does rain fall?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.277,
            0.39,
            0.664,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "**I wonder, ponder and dream each day, As water's journey takes its way.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.628,
            0.156,
            0.88,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.485,
            0.871,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "Activity 8.10 demonstrates the role of dust particles in the formation of clouds."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.536,
            0.196,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.538,
            0.76,
            0.562
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 8.10: Let us engage in a group activity"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.091,
            0.591,
            0.228,
            0.651
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Caution Handle burning paper carefully."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.571,
            0.882,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": " Take an empty discarded one litre plastic bottle. Pour about one cup of water into it."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.616,
            0.883,
            0.678
          ],
          "content": " Close the lid tightly. Now quickly squeeze and release the bottle continuously for about 2–3 minutes. Observe the space above the water in the bottle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.681,
            0.883,
            0.723
          ],
          "content": " Repeat the same activity after adding a small burnt piece of newspaper into the water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.725,
            0.553,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": " What will you observe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.749,
            0.882,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "In this case, you will observe some haziness (clouds) above the water in the bottle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.794,
            0.883,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": " The burnt newspaper provides very small invisible dust particles, around which water vapour condenses and forms clouds."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.859,
            0.883,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": "Let us perform Activity 8.11 to represent our understanding of how water changes its state and its movement."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
